    fix(test): poll for the child-written PID file in the arch002 start test
    
    Foreman follow-up to 8cb2f5b0. The first ARCH-002 test still asserted
    `fs.pathExists(PID_FILE)` immediately after `start -d` returned, but the PID file
    is written by the DETACHED CHILD (`writePidFile` in bin/speclangd), not by the
    parent that exits. That is the same runner-speed dependency the rest of the file
    just dropped: on a cold 2-core runner the child can lose the race before it even
    loads, so the test would flake in the opposite direction from the status test.
    
    Now it uses the file's own `waitForPidFile` helper (20s bounded poll) and, as a
    strictly stronger assertion, checks the polled PID equals the PID the parent
    reported on stdout. Budget 10s -> 30s to match the bounded deadline.
    
    Verified on the merged tree at loadavg ~114 (16 cores):
      npx vitest run tests/daemon/arch002-background-daemon.test.ts  3 consecutive
      runs -> Test Files 1 passed (1) / Tests 4 passed (4)
      npm run build -> 0, npx tsc --noEmit -> 0
      npm test -> exit 0, Test Files 111 passed | 4 skipped (115),
                  Tests 1937 passed | 58 skipped (1995)
    
    Task: UX-002
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
